** The falling meteor visual effects and the sound during the {{#var:Chaos Meteor value5}} seconds effect delay are visible and audible to everyone.

* Chaos Meteor provides {{#var:Chaos Meteor value12}} radius [[flying vision]] while it is rolling. This vision does not last.
** Also provides the same vision for 3 seconds after reaching its final destination.

* With the cast range, travel distance, and effect radius, it can hit units up to {{calc|v1+{{#var:Chaos Meteor value1}}+{{#var:Chaos Meteor value2}}|v1={{#var:Chaos Meteor value3}}}} range away. The area between Invoker and the targeted point is unaffected.

* Chaos Meteor rolls at a speed of {{#vardefineecho:Chaos Meteor speed|300}} and always rolls the full distance, so it takes {{calc|v1/{{#var:Chaos Meteor speed}} round2|v1={{#var:Chaos Meteor value3}}}} seconds to reach the max distance.

* After landing, the meteor deals its main damage and places the burn debuff to units within its effect radius in 0.5-second intervals, starting immediately upon landing. 
** On each interval, the meteor first applies the damage, then the debuff.
** The main damage and burn debuff is applied separately, but they each can hit a unit up to {{#var:meteor max instances}}/{{ValueColor|1|{{#var:meteor max instances aghs}}|aghs}} times.

* The following Chaos Meteor damage calculations are all [[before reductions]]:
** The main damage can deal up to {{calc|v1*v2|v1={{#var:Chaos Meteor value7}}|v2={{#var:meteor max instances}}}} damage.

* The burn debuff deals damage in 1-second intervals, starting 1 second after the debuff is placed, resulting in {{#var:Chaos Meteor value9}} instances for each debuff.
** The burn debuffs from each interval fully stack and do not refresh each other.
** One instance of the burn debuff can deal up to {{calc|v1*{{#var:Chaos Meteor value9}}|v1={{#var:Chaos Meteor value8}}}} damage.
** All possible instances of burn damage per unit together can deal up to {{calc|v1*{{#var:Chaos Meteor value9}}*v2|v1={{#var:Chaos Meteor value8}}|v2={{#var:meteor max instances}}}} damage.

* Therefore, the whole Chaos Meteor, main and burn damage, can deal up to {{calc|(v1+v2*{{#var:Chaos Meteor value9}})*v3|v1={{#var:Chaos Meteor value7}}|v2={{#var:Chaos Meteor value8}}|v3={{#var:meteor max instances}}}} damage when a unit is hit by all possible instances.

* {{cf|Talnotes}} {{ValueColor|1|{{#expr:{{#var:Chaos Meteor value4 tal}}-{{#var:Chaos Meteor value4}}}}|20tal}} extra meteors are now launched with a {{ValueColor|1|{{#var:Chaos Meteor value11 tal}}|20tal}} angle to the left and right of Invoker.
** The angle is based on Invoker's position. No matter the cast distance, the meteors always land and travel along offset by {{ValueColor|1|{{#var:Chaos Meteor value11 tal}}|20tal}} from the centered meteor.
** The extra meteors land so that they are at least {{ValueColor|1|{{#var:Chaos Meteor value10 tal}}|20tal}} range away from the centered meteor.
** This means when the targeted point is within {{ValueColor|1|{{#expr:{{#var:Chaos Meteor value10 tal}}/tan({{#explode:{{#var:Chaos Meteor value11 tal}}|°}}*pi/180) round0}}|20tal}} range of Invoker, they land further ahead of the centered meteor to keep a minimum distance of {{ValueColor|1|{{#var:Chaos Meteor value10 tal}}|20tal}}.
** This means, unlike the centered meteor, the extra meteors cannot land within {{ValueColor|1|{{#expr:{{#var:Chaos Meteor value10 tal}}/sin({{#explode:{{#var:Chaos Meteor value11 tal}}|°}}*pi/180) round0}}|20tal}} range of Invoker.

* {{cf|expr}}
** Travel distance: <code>300 + 150 × {{Wex}} + (15 × [[w:Floor and ceiling functions|⌊]]0.5 × ({{Wex}} + 1)⌋)</code>
** Travel distance bonus: {{cf|Level|8}} <code>ΣTravelDistance + 15</code>
** Main damage per interval: <code>30 + (25 × {{Exort}})</code>
** Main damage per interval bonus: {{cf|Level|8}} <code>ΣMainDamagePerInterval + 15</code>
** Burn damage per second: <code>5 + (5 × {{Exort}})</code>
